---
/* /impressum — the provider identification § 5 DDG requires of a German site.
 *
 * German rather than English at the top, and at `/impressum` rather than at
 * `/legal-notice`, because the law is about being *found*: § 5 DDG wants the
 * information "leicht erkennbar, unmittelbar erreichbar und ständig verfügbar",
 * and the word a German reader looks for in a footer is the one word this page
 * is called. An English translation follows it, because everything else on this
 * site is in English and the reader who needs the address is as likely to be in
 * Utrecht as in Munich — but the statutory text is the German, and the English
 * says so rather than pretending to be a second original.
 *
 * The footer link is labelled "Legal Notice (Impressum)" for the same reason
 * the page is bilingual, and the parenthesis is the load-bearing half: a German
 * reader scans a footer for that word, and recognisability under § 5 is judged
 * against them. **Not "Imprint"** — in English an imprint is a publisher's
 * brand, so the literal translation is a word neither audience is looking
 * for.
 *
 * Written into the page rather than rendered from `docs/site/`, which is where
 * the privacy policy comes from. That document is there for a stated reason —
 * it claims things about what the application does with a microphone and a
 * socket, and a claim like that belongs beside the code that has to keep it
 * true. An Impressum claims nothing about the software. It is a fact about who
 * publishes the website, it changes when a person moves house rather than when
 * a release ships, and putting it in `docs/` would publish it into the manual's
 * content collection for no benefit at all.
 *
 * **Three things are deliberately absent, and each of them is the kind of thing
 * a well-meaning edit puts back:**
 *
 *   - **The EU Online Dispute Resolution link.** Every German Impressum
 *     template still carries `ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr`. The platform was
 *     shut down on 20 July 2025 and the address no longer resolves to it. A
 *     dead link to a body that no longer exists is worse than no link, because
 *     it is presented as a route a reader has.
 *   - **A VAT identification number.** § 5 Abs. 1 Nr. 6 DDG asks for one *if
 *     there is one*. Stating that there is none is a claim about somebody's tax
 *     status, and this page states no fact it cannot stand behind.
 *   - **The four paragraphs of Haftungsausschluss boilerplate.** "Haftung für
 *     Inhalte", "Haftung für Links", and the rest are a restatement of §§ 7–10
 *     DDG, which apply whether or not a page recites them. What is here instead
 *     is the one thing about this site that is *not* generic: what it links to,
 *     and under which licences its parts are published.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { pageSchema } from '../lib/schema.mjs';
import '../styles/docs.css';
import { sourceUrl } from '../lib/docs.mjs';

const SOURCE = 'website/src/pages/impressum.astro';

const description =
  'Provider identification for open-audio-analyzer.com under § 5 DDG: the ' +
  'name, postal address and contact details of the person who publishes the ' +
  'site, in German and in English.';
---

<Base
  title="Impressum — Open Audio Analyzer"
  description={description}
  path="/impressum"
  slimFooter
  schema={pageSchema({ title: 'Impressum', description, path: '/impressum' })}
>
  <div class="shell legal">
    <article class="legal-main">
      <div class="doc-head">
        <p class="label">Legal</p>
        <a class="doc-src" href={sourceUrl(SOURCE)} rel="noopener">{SOURCE} ↗</a>
      </div>

      <h1 class="doc-title">Impressum</h1>
      <p class="doc-blurb">
        Anbieterkennzeichnung für open-audio-analyzer.com nach § 5 DDG und § 18 Abs. 2 MStV.
        <span lang="en">An English translation follows the German.</span>
      </p>

      <div class="md" lang="de">
        <h2>Angaben gemäß § 5 DDG</h2>

        <address class="legal-address">
          Jonas Grunau<br />
          Zypressenweg 9<br />
          85551 Kirchheim<br />
          Deutschland
        </address>

        <h2>Kontakt</h2>

        <address class="legal-address">
          Telefon: <a href="tel:+4917632669958">+49 176 32669958</a><br />
          E-Mail: <a href="mailto:grunaujonas@gmail.com">grunaujonas@gmail.com</a>
        </address>

        <p>
          Eine E-Mail wird gelesen und beantwortet. Technische Fragen zur Software gehören
          allerdings besser in ein <a href="https://github.com/JonasGrunau/open_audio_analyzer/issues" rel="noopener">Issue</a>,
          wo die nächste Person die Antwort auch findet.
        </p>

        <h2>Verantwortlich für den Inhalt nach § 18 Abs. 2 MStV</h2>

        <address class="legal-address">
          Jonas Grunau<br />
          Zypressenweg 9<br />
          85551 Kirchheim<br />
          Deutschland
        </address>

        <h2>Zu dieser Website</h2>

        <p>
          Open Audio Analyzer ist freie Software und wird kostenlos abgegeben. Auf dieser Website
